    "created_at": "2018-04-15T17:18:15Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-04-15T17:18:15Z",
    "body": "> If dep.js contains import './index', it imports https://cdn.com/react@1.2.3/index.\r\n\r\n`https://cdn.com/react@1.2.3/index.js` is then instantiated and executed in the module map twice, once as `https://cdn.com.react` (the one the user imported) and a second time as `https://cdn.com/react@1.2.3/index.js` (the one `./dep.js` sees). This one edge case thus makes the entire approach fall over as it will fail on some packages.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
